#### 2.1.2 SessionManager (Singleton)

**Location**: [Controllers/SessionManager.java](file:///c:/Users/Ahmed/IdeaProjects/Online-Book-Store/src/main/java/com/example/onlinebookstore/Controllers/SessionManager.java)

**Responsibility**: Maintains the currently logged-in user's session across all controllers and views.

**Complete Implementation**:

```java
package com.example.onlinebookstore.Controllers;

import com.example.onlinebookstore.Models.User;

/**
 * Singleton class to manage user session throughout the application
 */
public class SessionManager {
    private static SessionManager instance;
    private User currentUser;
    
    private SessionManager() {
        // Private constructor for singleton
    }
    
    public static SessionManager getInstance() {
        if (instance == null) {
            instance = new SessionManager();
        }
        return instance;
    }
    
    public void setCurrentUser(User user) {
        this.currentUser = user;
    }
    
    public User getCurrentUser() {
        return currentUser;
    }
    
    public boolean isLoggedIn() {
        return currentUser != null;
    }
    
    public void clearSession() {
        this.currentUser = null;
    }
}
```

**Usage in Controllers**:

```java
// In LoginController
public void handleLogin() {
    User user = facade.login(username, password);
    if (user != null) {
        SessionManager.getInstance().setCurrentUser(user);
        // Navigate to appropriate dashboard
    }
}

// In any Controller
public void initialize() {
    User currentUser = SessionManager.getInstance().getCurrentUser();
    if (currentUser != null) {
        welcomeLabel.setText("Welcome, " + currentUser.getUsername());
    }
}

// On Logout
public void handleLogout() {
    SessionManager.getInstance().clearSession();
    // Navigate to login screen
}
```

**Benefits**:
- ✓ Consistent session state across all views
- ✓ Eliminates need to pass user object between controllers
- ✓ Centralized authentication state
- ✓ Easy logout implementation
- ✓ Prevents multiple session instances

**Session Workflow**:

```
1. User logs in → LoginController authenticates
2. LoginController calls SessionManager.setCurrentUser(user)
3. Navigate to CustomerDashboard/AdminDashboard
4. Dashboard calls SessionManager.getCurrentUser() to display info
5. User logs out → SessionManager.clearSession()
6. Navigate back to login screen
```

**[PLACEHOLDER: SessionManager Sequence Diagram]**

---

### Singleton Pattern Benefits Summary

| Aspect | DatabaseManager | SessionManager |
|--------|----------------|----------------|
| **Single Instance** | One DB connection | One user session |
| **Global Access** | All DAOs | All Controllers |
| **Thread Safety** | Synchronized | Not needed (single-threaded UI) |
| **Resource Management** | Connection pool | User data |

